---
<?php
require_once "$docroot/plugins/zfs.snapshot.manager/include/lib.php";

$enabled = zsm_is_enabled();
$csrfToken = isset($var['csrf_token']) ? (string) $var['csrf_token'] : '';
?>

<p>Hier wird nur festgelegt, ob der Snapshot Manager aktiv ist. Die Snapshots selbst verwaltest Du über den Hauptreiter <strong>Snapshots</strong>.</p>

<form markdown="1" id="zsm-settings-form" method="post">
  <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<?=zsm_h($csrfToken)?>">
ZFS Snapshot Manager aktivieren:
: <select id="zsm-enabled" name="enabled">
  <option value="yes" <?=$enabled ? 'selected' : ''?>>Ja</option>
  <option value="no" <?=$enabled ? '' : 'selected'?>>Nein</option>
  </select>

&nbsp;
: <span class="inline-block">
    <input id="zsm-apply" type="submit" value="Anwenden" disabled>
    <input type="button" value="Fertig" onclick="done()">
  </span>
</form>

<p id="zsm-settings-message" class="notice" style="display:none"></p>

<script>
$(function () {
  $('#zsm-settings-form').on('submit', function (event) {
    event.preventDefault();

    var button = $('#zsm-apply');
    var message = $('#zsm-settings-message');
    button.prop('disabled', true).val('Wird gespeichert...');
    message.hide().removeClass('warning').text('');

    $.ajax({
      url: '/plugins/zfs.snapshot.manager/include/settings.php',
      method: 'POST',
      dataType: 'json',
      data: $(this).serialize()
    }).done(function (response) {
      message.text(response.message).show();
      window.setTimeout(function () { window.location.reload(); }, 500);
    }).fail(function (xhr) {
      var response = xhr.responseJSON || {};
      message.addClass('warning').text(response.message || 'Die Einstellung konnte nicht gespeichert werden.').show();
      button.prop('disabled', false).val('Anwenden');
    });
  });

  $('#zsm-enabled').on('change', function () {
    $('#zsm-apply').prop('disabled', false);
  });
});
</script>
